    "date": "2007-06-07",
    "description": "Well, there's not much to say, just a great game made by Iwatani himself in 2007, which I know looks good, to be honest.<br /><br />Pac-Man Championship Edition (\u30d1\u30c3\u30af\u30de\u30f3 \u30c1\u30e3\u30f3\u30d4\u30aa\u30f3\u30b7\u30c3\u30d7\u30a8\u30c7\u30a3\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3 Pakkuman Chanpionshippu Edishon, sometimes referred to simply as Pac-Man C.E.) is a 2007 video game in the Pac-Man series developed by Namco Bandai Games. The game was designed by T\u014dru Iwatani, the creator of the original 1980 Pac-Man, and is Iwatani's last game before his retirement. Though originally released for the Xbox 360\u00a0via the Xbox Live Arcade service, Championship Edition was later released for iOS and Android platforms, and on the PlayStation Network for the PlayStation Portable and PlayStation 3. A sequel to the game called Pac-Man Championship Edition DX was released in 2010.<br /><br />In this post you find these game versions:<div><b>Android, iOS, PSP, Xbox 360, Nintendo 3DS, NES</b><br /><br />However, the remaining ones:\u00a0<b>Roku, Maemo, PS3.\u00a0</b>Are not available for the moment<br /><br />For the Nintendo 3DS rom file, well, the thing is that the game is included in the game <b>Pac-Man &amp; Galaga Dimensions</b>\u00a0game so yeah, that means if you install this game, you may have the pac-man championship edition in the game itself and you can download <a href=\"https://romsfun.com/download/pac-man-galaga-dimensions-43288\" rel=\"ugc nofollow\">here</a>.</div>",
